configuration                                  warps instr/kk smem bytes  FLOP/B warp FLOP/B block
F6-23 vec 128x128 (FP32, 1 instr = 1 FMA)          8    16384       8192          7.1         32.0
F6-24 dbuf 64x64  (FP32)                           8     4096       8192          3.6         16.0
F6-26 wmma 64x64  (FP16, 16x16x16, no smem)        4        4          0         16.0         32.0
example 128x128x32 (FP16, 16x8x16, 3 stages)       4       64      49152         32.0         64.0
warp tile of the F6-23/F6-24 kernels: tid / (BN/TN) picks the rows, so one warp covers 32/(BN/TN) thread rows across the whole BN
instr/kk = instruction tiles per warp per BK step; FLOP/B warp = operations per operand byte all warps read per step; FLOP/B block = per byte the block brings in from global memory
